A||||5||JJ||If I buy it, how do I tweek it?
Z||000000||JJ||03-23-99||09:38 PM||||   Im thinking about buying a fiero to race in SOLO II. I found a nice '88 coupe. Although its only a 4cyl :-( its priced at only 1300. The owner says it needs rear rotors, a clutch and an O2 sensor to be mint. Is this a good deal? Would this be a good car to race? <br>I researched the I-4 a little to find that there are virtually no aftermarket parts that I could find to be competative in SP. Not even a good exhaust. Are there any good mods for the I-4? If I wanted to swap out for a V6, could I get money for the 4cyl at the same time? How much would it cost then? <br>Any advise is appreciated! <br>JJ
Z||000001||Punkndrublic||03-24-99||11:08 PM||||The best advise that i could give you is to totally drop the stock four, The whole thing is weak. You use to beable to buy the SD-4 block, rods, crank, pistons etc. from Pontiac but im not sure if their available anymore. Its the one they put in the indy pace car, supposedly the hp just kept increasing the more the engine broke in, up 500 or something.
Z||000002||Pretender||03-25-99||04:23 AM||||do all the indy fiero's have the sd4? or is it just a select few?...was that up to 500hp?...thats 300 more hp then the sd4 comes w/....i think i read that in an old pontiac mag. 
Z||000003||HF6582||03-26-99||12:53 AM||||a basic super duty 4 engine build will<br>bring in around 205-225 hp.<p>the sd4 was never in a generally availlable<br>production car.
Z||000004||Punkndrublic||03-26-99||08:07 PM||||The 500 hp came from some magazine or something that i was reading long time ago, bout the actually engine that the REAL pace car, the one on the track, not the replicas that the public could buy in 84.
Z||000005||theogre||03-28-99||04:03 PM||||check the rules for that class.... only certain mods are allowed as I recall.<p>Assuming it's alowed... at the very least:<p>Upgrade the brakes to vented rotors.<br>Replace ALL suspension bushings.<br>Replace the cradle bushings.<br>Replace the motor mounts and dog bone.<p>replace the bushings/mounts/dogbone with urethane where allowed. Replace the cradle bushings with aluminum where allowed.
